                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i2">
                            <locus from="36v" to="67v"/>
                            <title ref="LIT1379edadab"/>
                            <note>Divided in paragraphs, numbered ‘1’ to ‘223’. However, the numbers ‘108’, ‘109’, ‘110’, ‘163’ and ‘184’ are erroneously
                                numbered twice, resulting in a total number of 228 paragraphs. A large number of traits are taken from the 
                                <ref type="work" corresp="LIT7530MashafaMad"/> next to many medico-magic receipts and magic prayers and a treatise 
                                on the medical and magic value of each of Psalms of David on <locus from="62r" to="67v"/>.  
                                (Cp. the Arabic treatise, which was published in <bibl><ptr target="bm:Khater1970Psaumes"/></bibl>).
                                Similar treatise appears also in other <ref type="work" corresp="LIT5048Hassabat#Psalms">collections of Ḥassābāt as
                                 ‘Calculus of the Psalms’ / ‘Ḥassāba Dawit’</ref>.
                                A similar, but different medico-magic collection with the same title is attested in BnF Éthiopien 648 (Collection Griaule).</note>
                            <textLang xml:lang="am"/>
                            <incipit xml:lang="am">የዋጊኖስ፡ ቅጸል፡ ወግጠህ፡ በደንዳናው፡ ጠምቀህ፡ ቅባው፡ ያሰምራል። ዓዲ፡ የልት፡ ሥር፡ ከነ፡ ቅጸሉ፡ ወግጠህ፡ በጠጅ፡ ዘፍዝፈህ፡ 
                                በራስህ፡ ደፍድፍ፡ ጸጉር፡ ያበቅላል። ፩ የሚያጠቁር፡ ጠጉርን፤ የልት፡ ስር፡ በፍየል፡ ሽንት፡ ያነፍረዋል፡ በራሱ፡ ይታጸባል፡ ልቱን፡ አሳርሮ፡ ደቍሶ፡ በፍየል፡ ሽንት፡ ለውሶ፡
                                ይታጸቧል፡ አደስ፡ ጨፍልቆ፡ በውሀ፡ ዘፍዝፎ፡ ቢቀቡት፡ ያጠቍራል። ፬ ለሽበት፡</incipit>    
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i3">
                            <locus from="67v" to="70r"/>
                            <title type="incomlete" ref="LIT2849RepCh131"/><!-- Issue #3415-->
                                <note>The first five stanzas are missing. The text begins with the last three verses of the sixth stanza, which are written in 
                                    continuo in the manuscript.</note>
                                <textLang xml:lang="gez"/>
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">ሩፋኤል፡ በመንፈስ፡ ወመልዓከ፡ ሕይወት፡ አንተ። ሴስየኒ፡ ለፀማድከ፡ ኵሎ፡ ዕለተ። ምስለ፡ <sic>ጽዋዕ፡ ጽድቅ፡</sic> እፁር፡ ማሕየዌ፡ ኅብስተ።<lb/>
                                ሰላም፡ ለአስናኒከ፡ አስናነ፡ መልዓክ፡ ግሩም።<lb/>
                                ወለልሳንከኒ፡ ግብረ፡ መለኮት፡ አዳም።<lb/>
                                ሩፋኤል፡ <sic>ግሩም፡ አንተ፡ ዕሩቀ፡</sic> ሥጋ፡ ወደም።<lb/>
                                ኢያዕቅጸኒ፡ መስገርቱ፡ ለአርዌ፡ ኃጢአት፡ ርጉም።<lb/>
                                በኃይለ፡ ዚአከ፡ እበትክ፡ አርክከ፡ ድኩም።</incipit>
